Problem 2: skycormednorm()
--------------------------
I wrote a function called skycormednorm() to subtract the normalized
median sky from an individual dark-subtracted object frame.

The function accepts:

1. a 2D dark-subtracted object frame,
2. the 2D normalized median sky frame,
3. an optional normalization region.

If no normalization region is supplied, the whole image is used.

The function calculates the median object level in the chosen
normalization region. This provides the normalization factor needed
to restore the normalized sky to the brightness scale of the
individual object frame.

The de-normalized sky is calculated using:

denormalized_sky = normalized_sky * normfactor

The final sky-corrected image is then:

corrected = object_frame - denormalized_sky

I made copies of the object and sky arrays inside the function so
that the input arrays in the caller were not modified.

I explicitly tested this and obtained:

Object input unchanged: True
Sky input unchanged: True


