Problem 3a: Gaussian fitting
-----------------------------
I used the class gaussian.py module to fit two-dimensional Gaussian
profiles to each of the three stars in each of the first three frames.

For every star/frame combination I:

1. copied an 11 x 11 subimage around the approximate position,
2. calculated and subtracted the median background from the copy,
3. used a 3 x 3 median-filtered copy only to improve the initial
   estimate of the stellar position,
4. fitted the original unsmoothed data with gaussian.fitgaussian(),
5. calculated the mean of the fitted y and x Gaussian widths,
6. converted the fitted subimage coordinates back to full-image
   coordinates, and
7. stored width, cy, and cx in the photometry table.

